## Drift from baseline

Both signals measure how far this endpoint's behavior has moved from its reference period (its first two weeks). LT tracks the average change in the returned tokens' log-probabilities (nats); B3IT tracks the total-variation distance of the border-input votes (0–1). Both read 0 when the endpoint matches its baseline and rise — staying elevated — after a real change.

